' UI-42 on the start screen: the window resized, and clicks at the edges of
' its controls landing on them, or just beside them, at each size; then the
' game, opened at the size the start screen's window was left (one window,
' as v1.2 has). Run with `menu seed 7 window 640x480`, as it is and with
' `newgfx off`. The pointer goes through the window's own transform here:
' `menuclick` is made a window pixel in the window as it is when the step
' is taken.
menuclick 160,100        ' the intro: a click goes to the start screen
wait 30
resize 1280x720          ' 1.5x: a 853 x 480 backbuffer, the screen centred in 455 x 213
wait 3
snap menu_1280
menuclick 12,163         ' a pixel left of NOTES (13,163 36x18): nothing
wait 3
menuclick 13,163         ' NOTES' first pixel: the notes open
wait 3
snap notes_1280
press escape             ' and close
wait 3
resize 1920x1080         ' 2x: 960 x 540, 512 x 240
wait 3
snap menu_1920
menuclick 48,181         ' a pixel below NOTES' last: nothing
wait 3
menuclick 48,180         ' NOTES' last pixel: open
wait 3
press escape
wait 3
resize 1000x700          ' an odd size: 1.5x, 667 x 467, 356 x 208
wait 3
snap menu_1000
menuclick 49,163         ' a pixel right of NOTES: nothing
wait 3
menuclick 60,104         ' player one's name field
menuclick 163,54         ' START
press escape             ' Back closes the manual v1.2 opens on a new game's first world map
wait 3
snap game_1000
save
quit
